{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1528182084,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM5NDYwMjk4Mg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2470#issuecomment-394602982"},"message":"The reason for this behavior is that annex is only needed once a successfully cloned repository is locally initialized. Prior to the clone we cannot know whether this is needed. Moreover, DataLad works with plain Git repositories too, hence we would not want to error on a missing or outdated annex right away.\n\nI see your point, but I don't think we can do anything about it, without complicating the situation even further. If datalad was installed via a system package manager (e.g. APT) it should always yield a working datalad+annex+git combo. If those pieces are installed from separate sources we cannot do much more than error as soon as we become aware of an issue.\n\nI am closing this now, but please feel free to reopen, if you see a viable path to get this issue addressed.","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1528182084,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50MTY2MjkyOTgxNA=="},"status":2},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1528182128,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDE2NjI5MzA4Mzg="},"added":["wontfix"],"removed":[]}]}